From 5609230be4b2e06ba632312d5e675fb54cf62f4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sureshkumar <suresure@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 18:59:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] [prplmesh] steering: fix MLO join/leave loop and BTM steering
 for MLO clients

- Introduce MLO-aware handling of disconnect events: track links
  individually and only trigger LEAVE when all affiliated links are
  disconnected. Avoid removing the MLD client entry on partial disconnects.

- Use the AP MLD identifier in association notifications for MLO clients
  to ensure correct interpretation and avoid false roam detection.

- Add logic to distinguish multi-link joins from actual roaming, preventing
  unnecessary disassociation when links belong to the same AP MLD.

- Ensure steering requests are sent through the correct link-specific
  interface to allow proper handling by the AP.

- Avoid sending silent disassociation during steering, as ACL-based blocking
  is sufficient and prevents confusion in multi-link scenarios.

- Ensure non-BTM-capable clients are still steerable by enforcing ACL-based
  blocking when needed.

Signed-off-by: Sureshkumar <suresure@qti.qualcomm.com>
